00:57:59.420 --> 00:58:00.340
I'm talking about Gilead,

00:58:00.380 --> 00:58:01.160
is a brilliant man.

00:58:01.740 --> 00:58:02.920
But with all of that,

00:58:03.020 --> 00:58:03.860
he's Ashkenaz

00:58:03.860 --> 00:58:04.880
and he has his own ways

00:58:04.880 --> 00:58:05.860
and I'm not to criticize

00:58:05.860 --> 00:58:06.460
the man because

00:58:06.460 --> 00:58:07.180
he is a Tamech.

00:58:07.860 --> 00:58:08.980
But I go into

00:58:08.980 --> 00:58:09.680
the son's house

00:58:09.680 --> 00:58:10.320
and I've been at

00:58:10.320 --> 00:58:11.280
the father's house also.

00:58:11.400 --> 00:58:12.120
They live close by

00:58:12.120 --> 00:58:13.320
and I'm their insurance man

00:58:13.320 --> 00:58:13.960
and they like me

00:58:13.960 --> 00:58:14.520
and I like them.

00:58:15.140 --> 00:58:15.920
I go into the house

00:58:15.920 --> 00:58:16.400
and they have

00:58:16.400 --> 00:58:17.640
pilaki,

00:58:18.140 --> 00:58:18.480
you know,

00:58:18.540 --> 00:58:19.660
all the way on this side

00:58:19.660 --> 00:58:21.240
for meat.

00:58:22.160 --> 00:58:22.880
Then another one

00:58:22.880 --> 00:58:24.060
all the way on that side

00:58:24.060 --> 00:58:24.840
for milk.

00:58:24.840 --> 00:58:30.100
I mean, they're not even close. I have two sinks. One's for meat, one's for milk, but they're part of the whole...

00:58:30.100 --> 00:58:31.920
But we never had two sinks. You had a...

00:58:31.920 --> 00:58:33.940
No, no, no. Let me get to the point. Let me get to the point.

00:58:34.180 --> 00:58:37.560
And they got two refrigerators, okay? And they have two stoves.

00:58:38.660 --> 00:58:41.140
I'm not sure about the two stoves. The two refrigerators, I'm sure.

00:58:41.960 --> 00:58:47.200
So I asked once, and then I begged off because I'm not there to hurt their feelings and everything else.

00:58:47.720 --> 00:58:50.980
I said, what did your grandfather have in Poland or in Russia?

00:58:51.900 --> 00:58:52.640
What did they have?

00:58:52.640 --> 00:58:56.340
they didn't have a refrigerator at all they're lucky you know what they ate was

00:58:56.340 --> 00:59:00.460
from day to day fresh whatever chicken meat was on one day a week you ate meat

00:59:00.460 --> 00:59:07.480
because Thursday morning they killed it and by Saturday it was gone okay and I

00:59:07.480 --> 00:59:13.920
said weird well the answer I get is because in this country we're able to do

00:59:13.920 --> 00:59:19.740
more and so we should do more I said what make life better or worse I'm not

00:59:19.740 --> 00:59:26.740
saying do less. My argument is not do less. My argument is stop making it so difficult

00:59:26.740 --> 00:59:32.740
to live that one generation or somebody from each generation or somebody is going to walk

00:59:32.740 --> 00:59:38.240
away from it and say, listen, you've complicated my life too much. Sure, I want to keep kashrut,

00:59:38.240 --> 00:59:43.240
but I have to first be able to afford the meat. Then I have to be able to afford two

00:59:43.240 --> 00:59:48.240
refrigerators and two sinks and two stoves or whatever it is.

00:59:48.240 --> 00:59:51.240
Maybe two maids to wash the...

00:59:51.240 --> 00:59:57.720
I said, this did not exist in the Vilna Garon, this is like nobody.

00:59:58.280 --> 00:59:59.560
They lived with what they had.

01:00:00.200 --> 01:00:03.700
Of course, you can live here better because it's easy to wash the things you have.

01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:05.620
It's easy to take care of things you have.

01:00:06.160 --> 01:00:09.720
But there's another thing, if I may, just on this point.

01:00:11.420 --> 01:00:14.080
To do more, fine.

01:00:14.080 --> 01:00:21.080
But to do more, you cannot just put three pairs of tefillin or four pairs of tefillin.

01:00:21.080 --> 01:00:22.080
Some people have two.

01:00:22.080 --> 01:00:26.080
Yeah, but I say, but not three, not four, not five.

01:00:26.080 --> 01:00:32.080
To do more, there are other misva in addition to basar v'halav.

01:00:32.080 --> 01:00:39.080
Basar v'halav, meat and milk, kamikazo, there is a maximum of six hours between them.

01:00:39.080 --> 01:00:46.080
them. What is forbidden is very clear, is to cook them or to be hot together or to be

01:00:46.080 --> 01:00:51.080
something else. All the other things is totally irrelevant. It's just like you say, I want

01:00:51.080 --> 01:00:57.580
to be more Shomer Shabbat, so I'm Shomer Shabbat until Monday morning. This is ridiculous.

01:00:57.580 --> 01:01:02.580
I begin my Shabbat on Thursday afternoon and I go through Monday morning. That is all ridiculous.

01:01:02.580 --> 01:01:07.680
It's not more Shabbat. Instead of this, there are other misva. Yes. And one of the misva

01:01:07.680 --> 01:01:12.400
I think is terribly important, I would like people in elementary school to think about

01:01:12.400 --> 01:01:21.400
it, is the old age homes, to go to the Zekeim and Zekeinot, the Yehoshua and Yehoshua, and

01:01:21.680 --> 01:01:28.680
to teach the children how to go to the elders and the poor and to go to their homes, just

01:01:31.040 --> 01:01:35.900
to be a company. You have to see sometimes old people, they would see the face of a young

01:01:35.900 --> 01:01:40.400
child and just just by seeing the face they they they they become time a team

01:01:40.400 --> 01:01:46.760
and then so on so there are many miss what that we could do besides adding two

01:01:46.760 --> 01:01:52.220
frigidus or whatever it is have their third figure for for all I you know the

01:01:52.220 --> 01:02:00.520
the one with the the new immigrant comes to Israel and he brings three frigidus

01:02:00.520 --> 01:02:02.520
Why three frigerators?

01:02:02.520 --> 01:02:04.520
When they make a layer from here.

01:02:04.520 --> 01:02:12.520
Yeah, three frigerators. One frigerator is for meat, fine. The other one, fine. And the other is for uncoated meat.

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:14.520
That's right.

01:02:14.520 --> 01:02:16.520
Yes, alright.

01:02:16.520 --> 01:02:18.520
Not to mix it up.

01:02:18.520 --> 01:02:20.520
Alright, so...

01:02:20.520 --> 01:02:26.520
Sometimes when we think, and I have conversations with friends sometimes about it,

01:02:26.520 --> 01:02:27.680
I think we're doing more.

01:02:28.520 --> 01:02:30.520
We're actually in the long run doing less.

01:02:31.180 --> 01:02:34.780
And the way I explain it is like, imagine your son is looking at you,

01:02:35.200 --> 01:02:37.820
and you're putting three refrigerators in your house.

01:02:38.260 --> 01:02:39.180
Okay, or two, whatever.

01:02:40.720 --> 01:02:42.840
Then he assumes that that's the law.

01:02:42.980 --> 01:02:46.960
Unless you define it to him and teach him, no, this is not the law.

01:02:47.040 --> 01:02:48.580
I'm just doing a little more than I should.

01:02:48.700 --> 01:02:49.260
But you know what?

01:02:49.280 --> 01:02:49.940
It's not necessary.

01:02:50.060 --> 01:02:53.560
But most parents, when they go through that stage, they don't bother teaching their kids that.

01:02:53.560 --> 01:02:57.520
So when they come to my house and the child looks at me or my house,

01:02:57.580 --> 01:02:58.420
and there's only one or two children.

01:02:58.420 --> 01:02:59.140
He's not a good Jew.

01:02:59.560 --> 01:03:00.280
He's not a good Jew.

01:03:00.380 --> 01:03:00.880
I can't eat there.

01:03:01.140 --> 01:03:04.980
So what we think sometimes we're doing better, we're actually doing less.

01:03:05.060 --> 01:03:05.500
That's right.

01:03:06.220 --> 01:03:06.700
That's right.

01:03:06.740 --> 01:03:07.680
In terms of a community.

01:03:08.420 --> 01:03:13.160
And then that could isolate the child, let down from a different Jewish community.

01:03:13.340 --> 01:03:13.660
Oh, can I say that?

01:03:14.100 --> 01:03:14.460
Yes.

01:03:14.680 --> 01:03:18.960
And maybe this guy is going to marry outside the faith or whatever it is, you know.

01:03:19.060 --> 01:03:21.480
And I think that's one of the problems that we've had with the Shechito,

01:03:21.480 --> 01:03:24.420
that this Rabbi and this Rabbi, oh, but this Rabbi is better,

01:03:24.560 --> 01:03:26.820
so that's why, you know, oh, your shkita is not good enough.

01:03:26.940 --> 01:03:27.920
That's what's happening.

01:03:28.920 --> 01:03:29.400
And what is it?

01:03:29.520 --> 01:03:30.980
Instead of unifying the community...

01:03:30.980 --> 01:03:32.180
This one is boy, or this one is that one.

01:03:32.180 --> 01:03:32.380
Yeah.

01:03:32.980 --> 01:03:35.300
Instead of unifying the nation, it's making it separate.

01:03:35.400 --> 01:03:36.040
Yeah, indeed.

01:03:38.420 --> 01:03:42.820
But this is what today Tora is becoming a tool

01:03:42.820 --> 01:03:47.040
to promote disunity and friction among Jews.

01:03:47.040 --> 01:03:49.320
and that's why

01:03:49.320 --> 01:03:51.900
I pain at that

01:03:51.900 --> 01:03:52.680
you know

01:03:52.680 --> 01:03:55.880
Jewish people

01:03:55.880 --> 01:03:58.320
want to be united today

01:03:58.320 --> 01:03:59.800
we need to be

01:03:59.800 --> 01:04:02.200
we need to be united and want to be united

